The notice above is OpenCombine's, and it covers the work this repository is
based on: <https://github.com/OpenCombine/OpenCombine>, pinned at
1c6f02c7ed8140c0ba7a783aaddb6e0685a0037b. It travels with these sources
unchanged, and it is the notice a copy of this software must carry.

This repository is a fork of OpenCombine, under the same MIT terms and with no
other claim over Sergej Jaskiewicz's work. The changes are ours, and they are:

- the core, the Dispatch scheduler and the Foundation integration folded into a
  single module named `Combine`;
- the C++ locking helper and its module map;
- the adaptations iOS 6 and earlier need, among them the run loop timer's
  tolerance read and set only behind `#available`;
- a layer of our own, `files/CombineKit`, that carries what OpenCombine does not
  have: `Publishers.Merge` through `Merge8` and `MergeMany`,
  `Publishers.CombineLatest` through `CombineLatest4`,
  `Publishers.CollectByTime` with `Publishers.TimeGroupingStrategy` and
  `collect(_:options:)`, the equality and hashing Apple's own interface declares
  in the open, and `Publishers.MapError`'s labelled initializer.

